    "heroSub": "The rhythm of tradition. Learn Bharatanatyam with devotion, discipline and grace.",
    "heroImg": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Bharata_Natyam_Performance_DS.jpg?width=900",
    "welcomeH": "Welcome to Nritya Laya",
    "welcome": "Rooted in the revered Kalakshetra and Thanjavur traditions, Nritya Laya is dedicated to imparting authentic Bharatanatyam education in the cultural heart of Chennai. Under careful guru-shishya mentorship, students of all ages cultivate geometric precision (anga shuddhi), rhythmic mastery (laya), and expressive depth (bhava), transforming classical movement into a lifelong devotion.",
    "story": "Founded in 2012 by Smt. Meenakshi Sundaram in Mylapore, Chennai, Nritya Laya began with seven devoted disciples practising in an intimate traditional courtyard. Over the past decade and a half, the academy has nurtured more than 350 dancers, earning acclaim for its uncompromising adherence to traditional grammar, musicality, and stage presentation.\n\nOur curriculum combines rigorous adavu training with comprehensive Carnatic vocal theory, nattuvangam recitations, and Sanskrit shloka study from the Natya Shastra and Abhinaya Darpana. We guide disciples from their first tat-tai-tam steps through arangetram debuts, state youth festivals, and prestigious national sabha platforms.",
    "philosophy": "We honour the timeless Guru-Shishya Parampara, where dance is taught as a sacred union of body, mind, and spirit. Training begins with firm grounding in the diamond araimandi posture and rhythmic stamping (adavus), progresses into the subtleties of the nine emotional rasas (navarasas), and culminates in the complete classical Margam repertoire.\n\nEvery student—whether a child taking their initial steps or an adult reconnecting with heritage—is encouraged to pursue technical excellence with humility, joy, and profound musical sensitivity.",
    "c1": "#8b5a2b",
    "c2": "#c8281e",
    "c3": "#c19a55"
  },
